00:00:00.146 --> 00:00:03.760
Speaker 1: David. I'm starting to see&nbsp;
headlines that Joe Biden's approval rating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:10.000
is collapsing. Is this true? So first, let's&nbsp;
answer the question about the approval rating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.280
Then let's talk about what's actually going on.&nbsp;
If you look at 538, Joe Biden's approval has only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.800
dropped like within the margin of error. When&nbsp;
I looked most recently, Joe Biden's approval on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.000
an average of approval ratings went from fifty&nbsp;
three to fifty one point five. That's a really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.720
really small change to say. It's statistically&nbsp;
significant yet. But let's imagine that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:39.760
true that Joe Biden's approval is declining a&nbsp;
little bit. I think there's a couple of things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.520
to think about. First of all, it might be more&nbsp;
important to look at disapproval than approval&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:52.560
on disapproval. Joe Biden's disapproval has gone&nbsp;
up from an average of 36 to an average of 43.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:00.640
My guess is that that's right wingers who have&nbsp;
shifted from having no real opinion to saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.600
they don't like what Joe Biden is doing, probably&nbsp;
in part because of the propaganda, particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:12.000
around vaccines and covid and masks that has been&nbsp;
spreading among right wing media circles. But I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.680
think in this case, it's a little more important&nbsp;
to zoom out. It's very common that a normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:23.040
president, not Trump, a normal president, comes in&nbsp;
with a relatively high or higher approval rating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:30.240
And then over time, their approval begins to&nbsp;
erode and their disapproval starts to go up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.040
Why is this a lot of this approval disapproval&nbsp;
stuff is based on has the president done anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.480
that you don't like? And even if you've&nbsp;
liked a bunch of stuff Joe Biden has done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.080
there will be some people where in February&nbsp;
Biden does something they don't like.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.800
They now disapprove and they're not going back.&nbsp;
And then in March, Joe Biden does something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.680
different that another little cohort doesn't like&nbsp;
and now they disapprove and they never go back. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:03.040
the erosion of approval throughout a presidency&nbsp;
is relatively common with Donald Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.080
He actually left office with the lowest&nbsp;
approval of his presidency. I think it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.040
twenty nine percent, according to I think it&nbsp;
was Gallup. So that's relatively atypical.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.480
Also atypical would be like for. George W. Bush&nbsp;
after 9/11 had like 80 something percent approval,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:27.280
that was a unique sort of circumstance that that&nbsp;
explain that. So it's not particularly concerning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:36.080
I think that there's a there is this gets me&nbsp;
back to Biden needs a major accomplishment this&nbsp;&nbsp;

